WEBVTT

00:00:00.880 --> 00:00:03.560
This programme contains strong language.

00:00:22.480 --> 00:00:28.520
London in the 21st Century.

00:00:27.680 --> 00:00:32.800
For the people who live here, it can be the best of times and the worst of times.

00:00:32.000 --> 00:00:42.640
This is the story of both in one place, of two separate worlds coming together on a bend in the river at Deptford.

00:00:54.480 --> 00:00:59.680
So that is actually a photo from the Penthouse.

00:00:59.200 --> 00:01:01.480
Bloody hell.

00:01:00.600 --> 00:01:04.160
Hang on, yours is that one, Mummy, isn't it, the first one?

00:01:03.360 --> 00:01:05.959
It's that one, I think.

00:01:05.200 --> 00:01:12.960
How incredible to have a breakfast above the city watching over everything and the lights, it must be amazing.

00:01:13.800 --> 00:01:25.400
Five years ago, Lewisham Council decided to sell a tower block on the river to private developers Berkeley Homes.

00:01:24.440 --> 00:01:27.800
This is where the old roof was.

00:01:26.960 --> 00:01:29.280
All completely changing...

00:01:28.520 --> 00:01:30.920
It's a dream, isn't it?

00:01:30.880 --> 00:01:38.680
Its council tenants removed and its 144 flats transformed to attract a new class of resident.

00:01:37.920 --> 00:01:39.920
Just feels lovely.

00:01:39.000 --> 00:01:41.840
It feels like on the riverside.

00:01:41.040 --> 00:01:46.120
I just can't believe it, just out there, Daddy, is the inner city London.

00:01:47.080 --> 00:01:51.440
They have to believe in the fact that it is changing.

00:01:56.640 --> 00:02:05.600
But this dream of urban living lies at the heart of the notorious Pepys council estate.

00:02:04.680 --> 00:02:07.400
What the fuck is wrong with you?!

00:02:06.640 --> 00:02:09.000
Stop pushing me around!

00:02:08.440 --> 00:02:09.919
Look, you guys.

00:02:09.000 --> 00:02:11.320
Lovely area, this, isn't it?

00:02:10.520 --> 00:02:14.760
Mouthing off at me all the fucking time.

00:02:13.800 --> 00:02:17.360
Who do you think you fucking are?

00:02:16.520 --> 00:02:19.680
A place with different rules.

00:02:18.760 --> 00:02:23.440
Let me tell you something - there is not enough fucking hit men about.

00:02:22.480 --> 00:02:27.000
Where a new Briton is trying to make a home.

00:02:26.360 --> 00:02:32.640
The most hassle I get is from the stairs, from the people, with the shock and horror.

00:02:31.680 --> 00:02:34.080
A patch on the eye, big beard.

00:02:33.240 --> 00:02:39.240
Strange, isn't it, you have this tower block in the middle and then all the way around it...

00:02:38.640 --> 00:02:41.920
Where life is tough.

00:02:41.040 --> 00:02:43.560
You don't want to see him when he's drinking, do you?

00:02:42.760 --> 00:02:45.720
He still loves you, he's still thinking about you.

00:02:47.400 --> 00:02:52.240
Where friendship can mean the difference between life and death.

00:02:51.520 --> 00:02:54.880
If I go to buy any drugs, kick me.

00:02:54.160 --> 00:02:56.560
You said that yesterday, didn't you?

00:02:55.800 --> 00:02:57.040
What did you do?

00:02:56.200 --> 00:02:59.080
You went and bought them.

00:02:58.160 --> 00:03:00.840
You didn't kick me, did you?

00:03:00.040 --> 00:03:01.640
Oh!

00:03:02.240 --> 00:03:06.240
And where wealth is no guarantee of happiness.

00:03:05.840 --> 00:03:08.640
It should be me who's crying, baba!

00:03:08.080 --> 00:03:11.760
Love grows, it will grow.

00:03:10.960 --> 00:03:13.240
Three years...

00:03:12.560 --> 00:03:15.280
You can't believe this beauty!

00:03:14.480 --> 00:03:18.240
..Two communities on one estate.

00:03:17.360 --> 00:03:22.120
It's beginning to appear that there's more sophisticated drinkers coming in.

00:03:23.520 --> 00:03:29.120
It's bringing a different kind of person here as well, like changing the whole feel of the place and...

00:03:28.400 --> 00:03:30.640
Recycling areas.

00:03:29.880 --> 00:03:32.280
Exactly.

00:03:33.080 --> 00:03:34.680
I think it's brilliant.

00:03:52.640 --> 00:03:53.920
It's practically south-facing, a gorgeous view.

00:04:04.600 --> 00:04:19.560
Eastways we've got the Dome, Canary Wharf and everything back that way, more than 180 degrees that whole view, and absolutely amazing.

00:04:19.040 --> 00:04:23.800
It's been really nice looking out at it over the years.

00:04:33.000 --> 00:04:40.680
In a city of 7 million people, it's rare to find yourself completely alone.

00:04:45.000 --> 00:04:48.880
I'm the last in the tower.

00:04:49.560 --> 00:04:55.840
Lewisham have sold to Berkeley Homes.

00:04:55.000 --> 00:04:57.520
Everyone has been moved out.

00:04:58.280 --> 00:05:05.680
The whole of the riverside is slowly being privatised.

00:05:04.760 --> 00:05:10.080
There are an awful lot of housing estates that do back on to the river's edge.

00:05:09.160 --> 00:05:18.160
Those bits of the estate that touch the river's edge are all being sold off to various developers, so, as far as fairness goes, no, I don't think it's fair, really.

00:05:17.280 --> 00:05:19.960
But it's change, isn't it?

00:05:19.160 --> 00:05:21.640
Progress.

00:05:20.680 --> 00:05:22.120
So they say.

00:05:27.520 --> 00:05:43.720
The forces of change have decided that the tower's life as a council block is over with all but one of its residents now removed to inner city estates, away from the river's edge.

00:05:44.880 --> 00:05:54.400
But Les Brookes, a professional clown, bought his flat off the council and is refusing to sell it back.

00:05:54.040 --> 00:05:58.520
I bought the flat because I wanted to try and stay here.

00:05:57.560 --> 00:06:14.240
In negotiations with the council over the past 18-odd months, they've been asking me to move out, sending semi-threatening letters, some more threatening than they actually are, but it's been for the last year, "Sorry we sold you the flat, we want it back now."

00:06:13.520 --> 00:06:18.880
And... over the course of the last year, the heating has been turned off...

00:06:18.320 --> 00:06:21.640
It's become a fight now.

00:06:23.200 --> 00:06:26.840
These are going to be luxury apartments.

00:06:27.800 --> 00:06:35.360
By staying here, a few years down the line, it's obvious that this property would be of value.

00:06:41.240 --> 00:06:42.320
Thank you, darling.

00:06:41.520 --> 00:06:45.360
Thank you very much, thank you for...

00:06:44.680 --> 00:06:48.040
The keys to my first home.

00:06:50.200 --> 00:06:57.360
There's speculations, I suppose, as to how this is going to affect the Pepys estate in general.

00:06:56.560 --> 00:07:00.760
Nobody's really going to be sure until it actually happens.

00:07:00.080 --> 00:07:03.160
This is going to be a private block.

00:07:03.440 --> 00:07:09.120
Over there the rest of the estate isn't private, it's a council estate.

00:07:08.480 --> 00:07:12.360
So you're putting private property right on the edge of a council estate.

00:07:11.400 --> 00:07:14.040
Will the two mix?

00:07:13.280 --> 00:07:15.040
I don't know.

00:07:17.280 --> 00:07:21.760
I don't think anybody else out there really knows.

00:07:35.240 --> 00:07:37.880
Someone's bashing the shop up.

00:07:38.080 --> 00:07:39.320
Morning.

00:07:38.400 --> 00:07:39.920
Morning.

00:07:38.960 --> 00:07:40.560
Oy!

00:07:45.640 --> 00:07:46.800
Get back off.

00:07:45.840 --> 00:07:47.840
What's going on?

00:07:48.920 --> 00:07:53.160
Mark, it's Lawrence, I missed my appointment with you.

00:07:52.320 --> 00:07:57.400
I fell asleep in the park and woke up with kids chucking stones at me.

00:07:56.520 --> 00:08:02.120
Get moving, they're on their way round to nick you, now fuck off.

00:08:01.240 --> 00:08:05.000
If I come in contact with one of these, it dies.

00:08:04.200 --> 00:08:07.880
I'm still a little kid at heart, but who isn't?

00:08:07.120 --> 00:08:09.040
What man isn't?

00:08:08.080 --> 00:08:10.880
What you doing in here anyway?

00:08:10.080 --> 00:08:12.960
You fucking don't want to do nothing, see that?

00:08:12.160 --> 00:08:14.080
Want to have a fight?

00:08:13.200 --> 00:08:15.800
Come and have a proper fight.

00:08:19.320 --> 00:08:25.240
For the Pepys residents, change is only on the horizon.

00:08:26.280 --> 00:08:36.640
But nothing stands in the way of progress and living in the past can block the path to a happy future.

00:08:43.679 --> 00:08:46.360
30 years old.

00:08:45.520 --> 00:08:47.760
Yep.

00:08:47.680 --> 00:08:49.760
Falling to bits.

00:08:49.080 --> 00:09:01.400
Arthritis in my fingers, a bad back, curvature of the spine... ..blisters and corns on my feet and going bald.

00:09:05.240 --> 00:09:14.680
As my old foreman, Matt, used to say, "Bearing up from the mental strain of modern living."

00:09:16.840 --> 00:09:21.000
Wayne Tapper has hit a crossroad.

00:09:20.240 --> 00:09:24.400
Do you think I should wear this dress?

00:09:23.520 --> 00:09:25.120
Yes.

00:09:24.400 --> 00:09:26.440
But they pop out.

00:09:25.560 --> 00:09:29.120
Take them clothes upstairs!

00:09:28.800 --> 00:09:35.920
A month ago the mental strain of hitting 30 and knowing it was time to settle down proved too much.

00:09:35.120 --> 00:09:40.680
So he walked out on his girlfriend, Kelly, and their two young children, Tiana and Tyrell.

00:09:41.520 --> 00:09:44.040
Tyrell, listen, are you listening to me?

00:09:43.360 --> 00:09:49.800
If I call here and find you have been a little mm-mm, you're going to get it, you understand me?

00:09:51.920 --> 00:09:53.880
I'm hungry, man!

00:09:53.120 --> 00:09:55.240
It's 7 o'clock.

00:09:56.240 --> 00:10:01.680
He's come back with a promise to be the father HE never had, to his kids.

00:10:01.920 --> 00:10:03.200
Come on, then.

00:10:02.280 --> 00:10:06.200
I need to tart myself up a bit more.

00:10:05.320 --> 00:10:09.000
Get my watch, it's on the telly, babe.

00:10:08.640 --> 00:10:09.960
Get it yourself.

00:10:09.120 --> 00:10:10.720
Please!

00:10:10.120 --> 00:10:12.000
Things to do!

00:10:11.200 --> 00:10:13.480
Please!

00:10:12.640 --> 00:10:15.320
It's your bloody fault for being at the PlayStation, innit?

00:10:16.400 --> 00:10:23.520
And on the seventh anniversary of meeting Kelly, Wayne is hoping they can make a fresh start.

00:10:23.960 --> 00:10:25.600
Phwoar!

00:10:24.800 --> 00:10:26.400
THEY KISS Shut up!

00:10:25.960 --> 00:10:27.640
Phwoar!

00:10:26.800 --> 00:10:28.000
Phwoar!

00:10:28.600 --> 00:10:29.840
Phwoar!

00:10:43.240 --> 00:10:45.680
Seven years, man.

00:10:44.760 --> 00:10:47.320
Yeah, you've been a right cow!

00:10:46.480 --> 00:10:48.800
You dickhead!

00:10:49.400 --> 00:10:52.120
Think about it.

00:10:51.440 --> 00:10:56.920
We went from homeless, we got evicted after we had Tyrell.

00:10:56.080 --> 00:10:58.840
How long was we in the hostel for?

00:10:58.240 --> 00:10:59.400
Six months?

00:10:58.480 --> 00:11:00.640
Six months.

00:10:59.720 --> 00:11:01.400
Jumping the trains all the time.

00:11:00.440 --> 00:11:04.560
Jumping the trains.

00:11:03.760 --> 00:11:05.640
Do you remember?

00:11:04.800 --> 00:11:06.600
Oh, later.

00:11:05.760 --> 00:11:09.040
We've come a long way.

00:11:08.720 --> 00:11:17.520
To celebrate, they have booked to eat in Canary Wharf on the other side of the river.

00:11:16.840 --> 00:11:19.080
This is really nice.

00:11:18.320 --> 00:11:20.640
Thanks, babes.

00:11:19.720 --> 00:11:22.480
Business class!

00:11:21.680 --> 00:11:25.960
"Buy, buy, buy, sell, sell, sell!"

00:11:25.160 --> 00:11:27.800
I can't believe, this is nuts.

00:11:27.760 --> 00:11:30.760
It is nice, isn't it?

00:11:29.800 --> 00:11:34.560
I've seen oysters for £1.60.

00:11:34.040 --> 00:11:38.640
"Farmed in the clear waters off the Irish coast.

00:11:38.080 --> 00:11:40.840
"Each additional..."

00:11:39.880 --> 00:11:41.320
EACH!

00:11:40.520 --> 00:11:42.440
Where are you reading?

00:11:41.600 --> 00:11:42.720
EACH!

00:11:41.800 --> 00:11:46.160
£1.60 - EACH!

00:11:45.200 --> 00:11:47.200
"Grilled..."

00:11:47.160 --> 00:11:49.680
I see that.

00:11:50.360 --> 00:11:53.240
21 quid!

00:11:52.400 --> 00:11:54.760
Give us a kiss, then.

00:11:55.640 --> 00:12:01.000
This is going to be one anniversary to remember, babe.

00:12:00.160 --> 00:12:01.400
Happy anniversary.

00:12:00.560 --> 00:12:04.520
Happy anniversary, babes.

00:12:15.360 --> 00:12:22.520
These past couple of months have made us grow up a hell of a lot, a hell of a lot.

00:12:21.880 --> 00:12:23.960
Life is better.

00:12:23.000 --> 00:12:25.600
We understand each other more.

00:12:25.480 --> 00:12:29.480
You did go a bit nuts, though.

00:12:29.040 --> 00:12:32.640
Wayne had a midlife crisis.

00:12:31.840 --> 00:12:35.520
It was, like, "Fuck it, I've had enough."

00:12:34.640 --> 00:12:38.720
You were a wanker because you left me to deal with it with the kids.

00:12:37.880 --> 00:12:42.520
I know because I was like going through what I couldn't handle.

00:12:41.600 --> 00:12:44.840
You were acting like a total idiot.

00:12:44.000 --> 00:12:45.840
Yeah.

00:12:44.880 --> 00:12:49.480
I was trying to do the best I could and take care of me and the kids.

00:12:48.600 --> 00:13:01.360
I know I wasn't dealing with it, but it was something from my parents and my background, which made me run away from the situations and run away from problems, which Tyrell doesn't have to do that.

00:13:00.640 --> 00:13:02.600
Tyrell's young, still.

00:13:01.800 --> 00:13:06.840
That's why we've got to drill it into his head that you can be better than that.

00:13:06.160 --> 00:13:10.600
You have to be careful how you drill things into kids' heads.

00:13:09.760 --> 00:13:14.000
There's bringing them up a certain way and there's brainwashing them.

00:13:13.160 --> 00:13:16.000
Yeah, but I want to brainwash them in the way that...

00:13:15.160 --> 00:13:17.440
No, why do you want to brainwash them?

00:13:16.640 --> 00:13:18.720
You are wrong there.

00:13:17.760 --> 00:13:20.000
That ain't wrong.

00:13:19.240 --> 00:13:26.680
It ain't about drumming it into the kids, it's about the way you bring them up, the way you treat them.

00:13:25.720 --> 00:13:26.800
Drumming positivity into his head.

00:13:25.840 --> 00:13:30.120
You don't need to drum positivity into no-one's head.

00:13:29.240 --> 00:13:32.760
At the end of the day, there's no point in dwelling on the past.

00:13:32.280 --> 00:13:34.960
You want me to start dwelling on the past?

00:13:34.480 --> 00:13:36.920
I can go on for ever!

00:13:36.040 --> 00:13:38.640
I'm not dwelling on the past.

00:13:37.800 --> 00:13:39.000
You are!

00:13:38.080 --> 00:13:41.560
Wayne, there is a time in your life when you need to get over things.

00:13:40.800 --> 00:13:42.160
Yeah.

00:13:41.320 --> 00:13:44.200
Well, get over it!

00:13:43.560 --> 00:13:48.840
All I'm saying is, right, how I was brought up...

00:13:48.600 --> 00:13:54.000
At the end of the day, the kids you are talking about are my kids as well.

00:13:53.320 --> 00:13:55.040
You're going on like I'm talking badness about them.

00:13:54.160 --> 00:13:56.720
I'm not.

00:13:55.960 --> 00:13:59.760
You're talking about my son and drumming it into, what?

00:13:58.880 --> 00:14:04.000
It's meant to be a family, not a cult.

00:14:03.200 --> 00:14:04.800
No, I'm talking about...

00:14:04.080 --> 00:14:08.520
Listen, I've had a nice meal, I'm not going to do sit here and do counselling sessions.

00:14:07.560 --> 00:14:09.760
It's not counselling...

00:14:09.120 --> 00:14:10.360
Well, stop.

00:14:09.720 --> 00:14:12.920
Why do you think you stopped drinking?

00:14:12.000 --> 00:14:15.560
Cos you turn into a prick when you drink.

00:14:14.600 --> 00:14:16.320
Am I being a prick?

00:14:15.480 --> 00:14:18.600
Yeah, you are.

00:14:17.760 --> 00:14:19.760
Really, am I being a prick?

00:14:18.800 --> 00:14:20.120
You are.

00:14:19.280 --> 00:14:22.040
I'm being a prick.

00:14:21.080 --> 00:14:22.560
You are not being fair.

00:14:21.760 --> 00:14:22.960
Oh, well.

00:14:22.000 --> 00:14:24.200
You are not being fair at all.

00:14:23.720 --> 00:14:26.880
You should be fair.

00:14:26.480 --> 00:14:30.160
Have a couple of drinks and you start going on like a bitch.

00:14:29.960 --> 00:14:32.760
What do you mean, like a bitch?

00:14:32.080 --> 00:14:35.400
You do this every time, mate.

00:14:36.720 --> 00:14:40.920
You just don't want to listen to this conversation.

00:14:40.040 --> 00:14:41.280
No, I don't.

00:14:40.440 --> 00:14:44.360
That's why we get into these arguments and these fights.

00:14:43.640 --> 00:14:44.760
I don't want to listen to it.

00:14:43.840 --> 00:14:47.640
I'm not going to listen to it.

00:14:47.440 --> 00:14:50.560
Sometimes I just don't understand...

00:14:50.200 --> 00:14:53.360
You are still going.

00:14:52.800 --> 00:14:54.400
Give it a rest!

00:14:53.440 --> 00:14:56.040
Seven years today.

00:14:55.400 --> 00:15:00.400
We're meant to be looking to the future, not going on about your past.

00:14:59.600 --> 00:15:00.880
You're not the only one who had it bitchy.

00:15:00.160 --> 00:15:01.600
Yeah, I know.

00:15:00.800 --> 00:15:02.800
Right, so give it a rest.

00:15:11.640 --> 00:15:18.640
When everyone tells you to let go of the past, it takes a brave soul to stand firm in the face of change.

00:15:21.000 --> 00:15:28.680
Lewisham wanted me out so they could complete the deal with Berkeley Homes.

00:15:27.960 --> 00:15:32.880
Thus begun the war of attrition to get me out.

00:15:32.080 --> 00:15:41.720
As part of my service charges, I should get caretaking service, a sweep, wash the corridor, bin room and lift.

00:15:40.760 --> 00:15:42.600
It hasn't happened in over a year.

00:15:41.680 --> 00:15:48.200
I pay for my heating throughout the year, but it's only turned on between October and February.

00:15:47.240 --> 00:15:50.680
I'm told it's too expensive to run just for me.

00:15:49.800 --> 00:15:54.600
A water main that supplied Aragon Tower has broken.

00:15:53.760 --> 00:16:01.040
It's now looking like I'm going to be without toilet, bath or hot water for over 21 days.

00:16:00.160 --> 00:16:04.240
My mail is going astray, at one point even stopped.

00:16:03.600 --> 00:16:08.400
I regularly post myself letters to make sure I have mail.

00:16:07.800 --> 00:16:10.440
Things still go missing.

00:16:09.560 --> 00:16:16.840
It's almost as if Lewisham is slowly trying to grind me down so I'll reach a deal ASAP.

00:16:22.480 --> 00:16:28.320
Clearly there's always going to be resistance to change and that's understandable.

00:16:31.880 --> 00:16:41.480
Berkeley Homes is part of Berkeley Group, which is one of the principal developers in London and the South-East.

00:16:40.680 --> 00:16:46.760
It's a company with turnover of approximately £1 billion a year.

00:16:45.920 --> 00:16:55.200
And we seek to be the urban regenerator of choice in terms of partnership with public and private bodies.

00:16:54.760 --> 00:17:03.640
Berkeley Homes specialise in urban redevelopment and currently have 150 building projects across the South-East.

00:17:03.240 --> 00:17:16.040
For the next two years the transformation of Aragon Tower into the Z building will be overseen from their headquarters two miles down the river.

00:17:15.400 --> 00:17:21.359
Split-level flats, a highly innovative, '60s design.

00:17:20.400 --> 00:17:27.000
The cladding will have to come off and the existing window system, we'll be replacing that completely.

00:17:26.079 --> 00:17:29.640
Right.

00:17:28.720 --> 00:17:35.480
'It's not specifically that we chose Deptford, 'Deptford had been identified as an area requiring regeneration.'

00:17:34.680 --> 00:17:38.200
This was one of a range of regeneration opportunities that were available at that time.

00:17:37.440 --> 00:17:45.000
We were attracted to this one because we thought the tower, although it was in need of refurbishment, was tremendously exciting.

00:17:44.160 --> 00:17:48.160
It's in a fantastic location, the views are stunning.

00:17:47.320 --> 00:17:53.320
In terms of the broader estate, we were impressed with the sense of community in that broader estate as well.

00:17:53.560 --> 00:18:01.160
Deptford is certainly a part of London which has a bit of a buzz about it and it's moving in the right direction.

00:18:02.160 --> 00:18:14.360
We don't want to try and segregate all the community from the new people we're bringing into the area, because that's the whole idea about regeneration, the new people will come in, they will be wealthy because they can afford...

00:18:13.440 --> 00:18:24.080
Buying into the dream will require a leap of faith and it falls to the marketing department to entice people into the unknown.

00:18:23.600 --> 00:18:33.440
..They will demand different things and they will want to live a different lifestyle, they'll want Costa Coffees, Italian restaurants and all the things that Deptford is slowly getting.

00:18:32.600 --> 00:18:39.960
The thing about the local area is cos that's such a negative perception of that, that is the main thing we have to try and overcome.

00:18:39.040 --> 00:18:44.880
I'll probably get Simon to do quite a lot of local area photography because that will really help.

00:18:43.920 --> 00:18:49.600
Deptford high street is quite cool and trendy.

00:18:48.760 --> 00:18:52.200
It won that award recently, I can't remember what it was for.

00:18:51.360 --> 00:18:54.440
Like the best high street...

00:18:53.480 --> 00:18:55.200
In Deptford!

00:18:54.400 --> 00:18:58.680
We talked about the area, they may see that as a negative.

00:18:57.760 --> 00:19:01.680
What can we use to basically enhance the area and show them that it's...?

00:19:01.000 --> 00:19:04.880
The views has definitely got to be the main thing.

00:19:04.080 --> 00:19:11.360
Pretty much uninterrupted, it is like a full panorama which is something you wouldn't get anywhere else.

00:19:10.920 --> 00:19:17.920
Greenwich is quite exciting as far as eating and drinking and socialising...

00:19:17.080 --> 00:19:33.320
We don't want to focus too much on Greenwich but it's saying these things are nearby, you can access them, without saying this is the only thing and ignoring the immediate area, but people love to think, "Where I'm going to live in the future is really up-and-coming."

00:19:32.440 --> 00:19:38.520
They can see their property is making money and that's what gets people excited.

00:19:37.640 --> 00:19:41.040
The day you get to take your first customers in there will be the best day ever.

00:19:40.840 --> 00:19:42.800
It will knock their socks off!

00:19:41.840 --> 00:19:45.720
The actual panorama that you get standing in...

00:19:46.200 --> 00:19:53.840
Let's have a little eyeball at this one.

00:19:54.240 --> 00:19:57.040
Did you look in this skip?

00:19:56.240 --> 00:19:57.520
You did, didn't you?

00:19:56.680 --> 00:20:00.720
They have to be emptied now.

00:19:59.920 --> 00:20:06.200
Regeneration offers much to the newcomer but it's only fair that the spoils are shared.

00:20:07.160 --> 00:20:10.880
See that thing there and other brass doings in it.

00:20:10.080 --> 00:20:22.120
Leol Gilbert spends his days scouring the estate for scrap metal from building sites, along with his best friend, Nicky.

00:20:21.240 --> 00:20:24.320
One of the few people I've met who you can trust.

00:20:23.480 --> 00:20:29.880
It's rare that you meet someone that you can trust them completely sort of thing, implicitly.

00:20:28.920 --> 00:20:31.560
That's it.

00:20:30.720 --> 00:20:33.720
I like those sort of people.

00:20:33.000 --> 00:20:35.480
Where did you meet him?

00:20:34.520 --> 00:20:36.360
In a skip.

00:20:35.960 --> 00:20:38.240
In a skip, yeah.

00:20:37.480 --> 00:20:40.520
I wonder who that is.

00:20:39.600 --> 00:20:41.920
Another Bob-with-a-barrow up there.

00:20:41.200 --> 00:20:44.760
Everyone's running around nicking our metal.

00:20:43.840 --> 00:20:47.640
We might not get lucky today.

00:20:46.800 --> 00:20:48.960
Not a bean.

00:20:49.360 --> 00:20:53.880
No big bits of cast iron or nothing we can purloin.

00:20:54.960 --> 00:21:01.320
Bumped into him in a skip, up the road, got talking and then we become friends.

00:21:00.360 --> 00:21:06.680
It is funny, innit, we can trust each other implicitly and neither of us nick off the other.

00:21:05.960 --> 00:21:09.600
It's weird.

00:21:08.960 --> 00:21:10.280
We clicked.

00:21:09.360 --> 00:21:13.680
It was skips, weren't it?

00:21:13.080 --> 00:21:15.680
But we clicked, like.

00:21:16.600 --> 00:21:18.960
Probably loads more in here.

00:21:20.640 --> 00:21:24.640
'Some poor bugger's got to climb in there.

00:21:23.840 --> 00:21:28.400
'It's going to have to be me because you got in last time.'

00:21:27.640 --> 00:21:30.400
Come to Daddy!

00:21:40.920 --> 00:21:44.200
There's more stuff over there, though.

00:21:45.200 --> 00:21:53.840
Metal from the skips is taken to a scrap merchant only 100 yards from Aragon Tower.

00:21:53.080 --> 00:22:02.600
They offer cash for scrap and the yard has become a source of income for a stream of alcoholics and drug addicts who live on the estate.

00:22:05.280 --> 00:22:11.080
Leol has depended on heroin for 25 years.

00:22:13.520 --> 00:22:21.360
Went through a period of not getting on with me mum but that is cos she was worrying about me and moaning every time she saw me.

00:22:20.400 --> 00:22:25.600
Then they went to this counselling session and it's changed her.

00:22:25.160 --> 00:22:40.400
Then she started, she came back and she would say, "Well, I can't tell you what to do because you are going to go away and do what you want when I'm not there "and can't see so me worrying about it ain't going to change that."

00:22:39.840 --> 00:22:45.160
With me dad, it's really hard to tell cos he don't show...

00:22:44.280 --> 00:22:54.680
Apart from once when I wanted to cash in my Premium Bonds and he had the hump cos I'd spent loads of money on drugs and I looked dreadful.

00:22:53.720 --> 00:22:54.760
Hmm.

00:22:56.600 --> 00:23:02.840
His words were, "You're killing yourself," and that was bad.

00:23:02.640 --> 00:23:05.160
Do you want to change?

00:23:06.320 --> 00:23:08.960
Yeah.

00:23:08.200 --> 00:23:17.000
Yeah, I could do a lot better... ..in every way, actually.

00:23:32.840 --> 00:23:47.440
If Wayne was to walk out, or we were to break up and I had to do everything here on my own, as a mother, if you have got kids, you have to carry on being a mum.

00:23:49.120 --> 00:23:53.360
Wayne's dad wasn't around, was he?

00:23:52.480 --> 00:23:54.360
No.

00:23:53.480 --> 00:24:02.000
Not being a bitch or nothing, but, at the end of the day, Wayne is my bloke and I take care of him as well but I cannot have no-one hold me back.

00:24:01.160 --> 00:24:09.840
And whether some people will see that as cutting your nose off to spite your face, or whatever it is called, I see it as taking care of business.

00:24:09.360 --> 00:24:17.640
Life is too short, I don't know what's going to happen tomorrow so I'm not going to sit around and wait for someone to sort themselves out.

00:24:20.200 --> 00:24:29.600
The freedom of a single life or together as a family - where does a man look to find happiness?

00:24:30.520 --> 00:24:42.600
It's the right message, the message of hope, the message of fulfilment, the message of God, the message of progression, the message of prosperity put into 21st Century language.

00:24:41.840 --> 00:24:46.680
The churches knew Jesus was cutting edge!

00:24:47.360 --> 00:24:54.880
Wayne spent the last month with his sister and she introduced him to the local Pentecostal church.

00:24:54.320 --> 00:25:06.640
They have a modern approach to attracting new members and he's been invited to the Birmingham Motor Show with the male members of the congregation.

00:25:05.800 --> 00:25:08.680
Let me borrow that mike and let them know that.

00:25:08.280 --> 00:25:13.360
See, I can't resist a mike at the moment.

00:25:12.480 --> 00:25:19.640
Fellas, there's a car you all need to see called a Range Stormer.

00:25:18.680 --> 00:25:20.080
OK.

00:25:19.200 --> 00:25:20.880
Oh, you've heard?

00:25:20.040 --> 00:25:23.040
The gospel has travelled!

00:25:22.480 --> 00:25:28.440
Now, possibly, we can all like take a day off Christianity and try and steal it!

00:25:27.480 --> 00:25:31.200
No, I'm only joking, that was a joke!

00:25:32.120 --> 00:25:38.960
...Be praying our Lord that as we journey, you will take us safely and bring us back again.

00:25:38.040 --> 00:25:42.280
We commit ourselves into your care and everybody says...

00:25:41.360 --> 00:25:43.000
AMEN!

00:25:44.640 --> 00:25:49.360
I think it's important for people to come and wake up.

00:25:48.680 --> 00:25:58.760
People often say once they plug into a dynamic ministry like the Tabernacle, once they plug into God, of course, they come alive.

00:25:57.960 --> 00:26:01.680
Lamborghini.

00:26:00.840 --> 00:26:04.560
Mine was the SLR Mercedes.

00:26:03.760 --> 00:26:06.800
I've told everyone about that already.

00:26:05.840 --> 00:26:08.400
Range Rover, I think.

00:26:07.520 --> 00:26:10.920
Have you seen the Porsche jeep?

00:26:10.040 --> 00:26:19.120
Women are a lot more socially interactive as far as sharing emotions, sharing innermost feelings; men, we tend to shut down a lot more, but events like this help.

00:26:18.280 --> 00:26:27.080
It's therapeutic when you can get-together with a brother, a guy and hang out and let the boys be boys.

00:26:26.560 --> 00:26:30.440
Excuse me, do you know what is the top speed of this?

00:26:29.560 --> 00:26:33.080
A top speed of 208 miles an hour.

00:26:32.120 --> 00:26:36.840
Faster than the Lamborghini then?

00:26:36.040 --> 00:26:37.960
Wow!

00:26:37.000 --> 00:26:40.200
Look at the boot space!

00:26:39.280 --> 00:26:41.920
You could fit a body in there.

00:26:41.120 --> 00:26:42.280
Go, go, go, do!

00:26:41.320 --> 00:26:45.080
I'll see you back at the firm, yeah?

00:26:44.160 --> 00:26:45.720
Oh...my... !

00:26:44.880 --> 00:26:46.520
Hold on a minute.

00:26:45.680 --> 00:26:47.400
Praise be, man.

00:26:46.480 --> 00:26:49.120
This is absolutely...

00:26:48.320 --> 00:26:49.600
Stonking.

00:26:48.840 --> 00:26:50.600
..Splendiferous!

00:26:49.720 --> 00:26:52.240
What be the price of one of these?

00:26:52.320 --> 00:26:56.560
The basic price for this car is about £292,000.

00:26:55.640 --> 00:26:57.360
Is that all(!)

00:26:56.520 --> 00:27:03.320
Just underneath you have the six CD changer and just underneath there is where the solid silver tumblers would sit.

00:27:02.520 --> 00:27:10.640
You've got all your controls here, this one is for the electric curtains which come as standard on both models for the rear.

00:27:09.920 --> 00:27:16.520
If you wanted them fitted on the side of the doors, you can, it's an optional extra.

00:27:15.680 --> 00:27:22.520
Can you imagine if God or Jesus was to design a car, could you imagine what it would go like?

00:27:22.040 --> 00:27:25.160
This has to be the kind of car God would want to drive in!

00:27:24.400 --> 00:27:33.360
Christianity is not just about materialism, it's about success, but God wants us to have material blessings as well.

00:27:32.520 --> 00:27:41.600
When you're able to see something, if I can conceive it in my mind, then I can have a career that can get me something like this.

00:27:40.680 --> 00:27:43.120
You can give yourself a goal.

00:27:42.160 --> 00:27:43.840
Of course.

00:27:43.080 --> 00:27:44.920
You enjoy coming up here today?

00:27:44.600 --> 00:27:47.320
Definitely, I'm glad.

00:27:46.520 --> 00:27:49.520
Men, we never talk to each other and that is the truth of the matter.

00:27:48.680 --> 00:27:51.760
Who invited you to church?

00:27:50.880 --> 00:27:52.200
Was it your sister?

00:27:51.280 --> 00:27:54.440
Well, admittedly, I was going through some problems.

00:27:53.640 --> 00:27:56.280
Right.

00:27:55.320 --> 00:28:03.840
And I ended up going to my sister's and the day I went to my sister's, that same day, she prayed for me.

00:28:03.280 --> 00:28:05.480
OK.

00:28:04.680 --> 00:28:08.240
She said she prayed for me and she was talking about the church.

00:28:07.360 --> 00:28:11.800
I thought, do you know what, it's time for me to start going.

00:28:11.040 --> 00:28:12.760
Right.

00:28:11.800 --> 00:28:16.560
I just felt the love, man, I felt the hope and everything.

00:28:15.760 --> 00:28:19.120
It felt good, it made me feel good as well.

00:28:18.280 --> 00:28:21.080
Like a new start as well.

00:28:20.240 --> 00:28:21.560
A new beginning.

00:28:20.800 --> 00:28:22.960
A new beginning.

00:28:22.120 --> 00:28:25.920
Everything in the past has gone.

00:28:25.200 --> 00:28:26.640
Yeah.

00:28:25.800 --> 00:28:28.680
I used to do lots of things, I used to take drugs, I used to smoke.

00:28:27.840 --> 00:28:40.400
Everybody has a past, everybody has some kind of issues that they need dealt with, and much like the seat of this car is massaging my back right now automatically because I've just realised...

00:28:39.440 --> 00:28:40.840
Is it?!

00:28:40.000 --> 00:28:42.800
Yeah, it is, it's massaging my back!

00:28:41.920 --> 00:28:47.600
God can relax you, he can make you wake up about life.

00:28:46.640 --> 00:28:50.720
You go from existing to start living.

00:28:49.920 --> 00:28:51.000
Yeah.

00:28:50.240 --> 00:28:53.640
Got two kids and all that, it's about time...

00:28:52.680 --> 00:28:57.880
At the end of the day if you love each other, if you've already spent some of your life together...

00:28:56.920 --> 00:28:59.800
Seven years.

00:28:58.880 --> 00:29:00.000
There you go.

00:28:59.040 --> 00:29:02.600
Seven, that's God complete number, seven biblically is his complete number.

00:29:01.720 --> 00:29:07.000
It's about time that some commitment went forward, a wholesome environment where the kids can be brought up.

00:29:06.480 --> 00:29:07.760
Yeah.

00:29:06.960 --> 00:29:09.200
Most definitely.

00:29:08.240 --> 00:29:12.960
Give them what you maybe never had.

00:29:12.320 --> 00:29:13.520
Definitely.

00:29:12.680 --> 00:29:14.880
That's another thing.

00:29:13.920 --> 00:29:17.760
Including a Bentley!

00:29:17.000 --> 00:29:19.200
You can do it.

00:29:19.240 --> 00:29:22.760
Dedication, as Roy Castle used to sing, dedication.

00:29:22.080 --> 00:29:23.760
Yeah.

00:29:28.680 --> 00:29:36.760
THEY LAUGH The road to salvation is often tough, and can mean losing the very things you love the most.

00:29:37.960 --> 00:29:41.480
Look, there's Donna.

00:29:40.520 --> 00:29:43.200
She's a pretty nice-looking girl.

00:29:42.280 --> 00:29:43.760
Oh yeah.

00:29:45.080 --> 00:29:56.800
Three months ago Leol's long-term girlfriend Donna left him, and moved out of his flat which lies directly under the gaze of Aragon Tower.

00:29:56.480 --> 00:29:58.960
You're never ever going to forget her?

00:29:58.360 --> 00:30:03.120
I picked her up and thrown her out before and she's always come back.

00:30:02.320 --> 00:30:06.080
At the end of the day, you can't... there's plenty more birds out there.

00:30:05.440 --> 00:30:07.360
Oh, of course.

00:30:06.560 --> 00:30:08.840
You know what I mean?

00:30:08.240 --> 00:30:09.760
Oh yeah.

00:30:08.880 --> 00:30:12.280
There ain't many nice as Donna.

00:30:11.600 --> 00:30:12.920
You can't keep that in your mind.

00:30:12.200 --> 00:30:16.000
You have to move further and find someone else.

00:30:15.240 --> 00:30:18.120
You're in love with her, so what?

00:30:17.720 --> 00:30:21.160
When you love someone like that, you don't change.

00:30:20.560 --> 00:30:26.000
It's hard to get out of your head, system, you think the world of her.

00:30:25.160 --> 00:30:27.880
I'll always think of the world of her, I always did.

00:30:27.040 --> 00:30:37.360
All you can do is go and find another bird, or girl I mean, sorry, you can't sit thinking "She'll come back to me, "will she come back to me?"

00:30:36.480 --> 00:30:39.440
You don't know, we can't tell.

00:30:38.800 --> 00:30:43.480
She can if she wants and she knows it.

00:30:42.720 --> 00:30:44.200
Whatever.

00:30:43.360 --> 00:30:44.680
I don't think she will.

00:30:43.800 --> 00:30:48.240
Yo u can't hang around forever.

00:30:55.960 --> 00:31:02.000
I used to have a friend that lived in Aragon Tower, they moved out.

00:31:01.200 --> 00:31:03.600
It's only Les now.

00:31:02.720 --> 00:31:05.800
A brave man.

00:31:05.080 --> 00:31:08.040
It's his property at the end of the day, he bought it.

00:31:09.960 --> 00:31:16.920
Really nice lifestyle, really fun, I want to see the girls interacting.

00:31:16.160 --> 00:31:22.680
It will be some time before Berkeley Homes have full access to the tower.

00:31:21.720 --> 00:31:22.960
Ooh!

00:31:22.320 --> 00:31:25.120
Look at that.

00:31:24.240 --> 00:31:27.320
There are dream homes being built elsewhere.

00:31:26.560 --> 00:31:28.640
It's lovely that, isn't it?

00:31:27.840 --> 00:31:29.560
That's fine.

00:31:29.880 --> 00:31:39.040
Basically what's happened is she's getting ready, just lolling about on the sofa and her friend comes in, drinking champagne, very lifestyley.

00:31:38.280 --> 00:31:40.320
Good.

00:31:39.520 --> 00:31:45.640
The purpose of this shoot is to try and... bring alive the brochure.

00:31:44.680 --> 00:31:53.480
We've built an exact replica of one of the apartments, we've got the exact kitchen that we're putting in.

00:31:52.640 --> 00:31:57.680
In fact the furniture that we've got here will go into the show home in a year or so's time.

00:31:56.720 --> 00:32:03.000
It's aspiration, trying to make people see what we are trying to create.

00:32:02.160 --> 00:32:07.880
Because we do our sales so early, you leave an awful lot to their imagination.

00:32:07.200 --> 00:32:12.640
So you are trying to encourage that imagination, you're trying to make them visualise living in the properties.

00:32:13.480 --> 00:32:21.360
In the apartments brochure it will be this shot, cut here, a bit of coffee, girl standing here.

00:32:20.640 --> 00:32:25.960
We'll take some shots of the girls drinking champagne, waiting to go out.

00:32:25.000 --> 00:32:26.120
Here?

00:32:25.280 --> 00:32:33.640
And then again here, "Investment in the Future", this might work being the girl on the laptop looking at her stocks and shares.

00:32:32.840 --> 00:32:34.760
Yes.

00:32:33.800 --> 00:32:35.760
That's really lovely.

00:32:34.960 --> 00:32:38.200
Head slightly more around this way.

00:32:37.400 --> 00:32:39.040
Round that way.

00:32:38.080 --> 00:32:39.680
OK.

00:32:39.840 --> 00:32:41.920
That's perfect.

00:32:44.760 --> 00:32:45.880
Mmm-mm.

