A visit from Donna to collect her post offers a last chance to redirect her affections.

00:34:43.639 --> 00:34:47.400
Come in, come in, please, beautiful, you look lovely.

00:34:47.679 --> 00:34:51.040
16 years we've been pals, yeah.

00:34:50.239 --> 00:34:52.600
A long time.

00:34:52.320 --> 00:34:55.199
I just don't...

00:34:54.360 --> 00:35:02.440
I can't live with anyone, I find living with anyone is impossible, don't matter who they are.

00:35:01.560 --> 00:35:04.680
Gentleman, no such thing as a gentleman.

00:35:03.760 --> 00:35:05.280
Yes, there is.

00:35:04.560 --> 00:35:06.720
You know there is.

00:35:07.320 --> 00:35:09.640
This is what I wanted to get...

00:35:11.640 --> 00:35:21.520
In the two years they were together, Leol and Donna spent all £30,000 of his life savings on drugs.

00:35:20.800 --> 00:35:23.800
Looks just like you actually, innit?

00:35:22.920 --> 00:35:25.640
Since she left him, Leol has been clean.

00:35:24.760 --> 00:35:29.040
Stop it!

00:35:28.520 --> 00:35:33.160
If I give Leol a 40...

00:35:32.680 --> 00:35:36.440
Leave some of it here, I tell you what to do, let me suggest this to you.

00:35:35.800 --> 00:35:37.760
No, you'll use it, Leol!

00:35:36.920 --> 00:35:39.840
I won't use it.

00:35:38.960 --> 00:35:41.240
Because I ain't got it.

00:35:40.360 --> 00:35:43.720
Donna, I've had it here for four days.

00:35:42.840 --> 00:35:44.160
I've lost a score already.

00:35:43.320 --> 00:35:46.400
Listen, I'm not going to spend your money, you know I won't do that.

00:35:45.720 --> 00:35:47.760
Keep that for me for an emergency.

00:35:46.800 --> 00:35:48.240
No...

00:35:48.000 --> 00:35:52.600
Give me that 20, yeah, and put 20 in for me and I'll get us one each now.

00:35:51.800 --> 00:35:54.280
I don't want to get one each.

00:35:53.360 --> 00:35:56.360
What do you want?

00:35:55.400 --> 00:35:59.640
No, I ain't been using because I go out with him every day and we've been too busy.

00:35:58.720 --> 00:36:02.200
I've been running around all day with metal in my hands and that.

00:36:01.240 --> 00:36:07.200
I ain't had a chance to use drugs, but that's good for me, I've been doing good.

00:36:07.040 --> 00:36:08.840
Oh, God.

00:36:07.920 --> 00:36:12.600
She goes so fast, everything's so quick.

00:36:13.360 --> 00:36:15.560
I ain't been using, mate.

00:36:14.600 --> 00:36:17.160
Stop a sec.

00:36:17.040 --> 00:36:21.360
I don't want to see you fuck all that money off in one go.

00:36:20.480 --> 00:36:26.760
I'll give you the key to the safe, you know I've only got the one key.

00:36:25.920 --> 00:36:29.280
You know I wouldn't spend your money.

00:36:28.320 --> 00:36:30.600
You should know me better.

00:36:29.760 --> 00:36:33.720
When my other cheques come make sure you look after them.

00:36:32.880 --> 00:36:37.960
Fuck me, if you can't trust me after all this time, who can you ever trust?

00:36:37.160 --> 00:36:47.600
This is mine and I want some so...

00:36:48.160 --> 00:36:55.280
I've got to go.

00:36:55.320 --> 00:36:58.920
You look gorgeous.

00:36:58.160 --> 00:37:00.080
See you later, yeah.

00:36:59.120 --> 00:37:01.320
Take care.

00:37:00.520 --> 00:37:03.360
I will walk down the road with you.

00:37:02.560 --> 00:37:03.960
See you later.

00:37:03.040 --> 00:37:05.160
Hang on a minute.

00:37:04.280 --> 00:37:05.920
I've got to go.

00:37:05.000 --> 00:37:06.200
I'm late.

00:37:05.320 --> 00:37:07.400
For what, the doctors?

00:37:06.560 --> 00:37:08.000
Yes.

00:37:07.120 --> 00:37:08.880
You've got ten minutes.

00:37:08.120 --> 00:37:12.280
If I'm five minutes late, they'll make me wait till six.

00:37:11.600 --> 00:37:15.560
I was going to say you've got 15 minutes to be late.

00:37:14.800 --> 00:37:16.920
See you later.

00:37:16.560 --> 00:37:17.680
Bye.

00:37:16.720 --> 00:37:18.720
It's hurt him.

00:37:17.880 --> 00:37:20.440
Hasn't it, really?

00:37:22.200 --> 00:37:24.320
It's hurt him.

00:37:23.640 --> 00:37:26.400
Go, have a talk to her.

00:37:31.280 --> 00:37:35.000
There ain't nothing to say, is there?

00:37:34.040 --> 00:37:35.520
Yeah.

00:37:42.760 --> 00:37:46.880
What do you want to do, get some more metal, yeah?

00:37:48.040 --> 00:37:52.120
Never met a bird like it, I ain't.

00:37:51.320 --> 00:37:56.440
She's the only bird I've ever met that I would have had a kid.

00:37:55.600 --> 00:37:57.840
He thinks the world of her.

00:37:56.960 --> 00:37:59.040
Everyone can see that.

00:37:58.240 --> 00:38:02.360
You've got to go for it and try and get her back.

00:38:01.400 --> 00:38:04.960
It's no good keep talking about her.

00:38:05.960 --> 00:38:09.600
What's your definition of romance?

00:38:08.880 --> 00:38:11.000
I don't know.

00:38:10.160 --> 00:38:13.040
I've never been asked that question before.

00:38:13.560 --> 00:38:16.480
She's the best thing that's happened to you?

00:38:15.760 --> 00:38:17.160
Definitely.

00:38:16.640 --> 00:38:18.400
Definitely.

00:38:19.160 --> 00:38:22.280
She helps sort my head out.

00:38:21.800 --> 00:38:24.440
She's been everything to me.

00:38:23.560 --> 00:38:28.960
She's been my girlfriend, lover, my mentor, my mother.

00:38:28.120 --> 00:38:33.240
I shouldn't let her be my mother but...

00:38:33.840 --> 00:38:38.840
Definitely a lover, I want to be with her... many more years to come as well, many, many more years to come.

00:38:42.880 --> 00:38:49.520
When the time comes to prove your commitment, actions speak louder than words.

00:38:50.320 --> 00:39:00.240
We went shopping... waiting outside the sports shops for him, thinking where is he, getting peed off with him cos he was taking ages.

00:38:59.280 --> 00:39:07.600
He come up to me and literally pushed me on the bench and got down on one knee in front of everybody in the shopping centre.

00:39:06.680 --> 00:39:11.840
I can't remember him saying nothing to me because I was so embarrassed...

00:39:10.960 --> 00:39:20.000
The only thing I remember he was getting Tyrell off his back saying, "Will you leave me alone, I'm trying to propose to your mother here."

00:39:23.080 --> 00:39:28.680
I was sitting in the corner of the sitting room and he comes in, he was gorgeous!

00:39:28.040 --> 00:39:31.640
Oh, gross.

00:39:30.880 --> 00:39:32.160
WAS!

00:39:31.320 --> 00:39:34.480
And that was it.

00:39:33.520 --> 00:39:39.000
After that, he serenaded me under the window.

00:39:38.200 --> 00:39:42.640
I could have went through your drawers!

00:39:44.240 --> 00:39:46.920
Where are you?

00:39:46.120 --> 00:39:48.720
I ain't got it on yet.

00:39:49.120 --> 00:39:52.000
I like your hair like this.

00:39:54.160 --> 00:39:57.440
SOBBING Oh, I can't cope with this.

00:39:56.600 --> 00:40:02.240
I was so strong when your brother got married.

00:40:05.040 --> 00:40:09.080
It's different when it's your daughter.

00:40:08.240 --> 00:40:10.880
I don't know why.

00:40:11.600 --> 00:40:13.760
Oh, it's beautiful.

00:40:13.080 --> 00:40:16.080
I can't say anything else.

00:40:24.560 --> 00:40:26.280
Mum.

00:40:26.520 --> 00:40:30.360
Tyrell, you cannot tell daddy.

00:40:29.640 --> 00:40:35.520
I didn't think this day was going to come, I thought she'd given up.

00:40:34.680 --> 00:40:37.720
Why can't we tell Daddy?

00:40:36.800 --> 00:40:39.080
It's a surprise.

00:40:38.120 --> 00:40:41.560
Because Daddy can't see it.

00:40:40.880 --> 00:40:47.200
When she was born she changed my life, that's the most beautiful baby I'd ever seen.

00:40:46.320 --> 00:40:55.480
She taught me a lesson when she says I'm going to live with a bloke, she broke my heart, because I didn't want any bloke to touch her.

00:40:54.640 --> 00:40:56.560
That was my little baby.

00:40:55.640 --> 00:41:01.080
Then I accepted the way she has been and accepted Wayne like a son of mine, you know.

00:41:00.120 --> 00:41:03.280
And now she's gorgeous, she is.

00:41:02.600 --> 00:41:04.480
Very gorgeous.

00:41:03.520 --> 00:41:04.720
Beautiful.

00:41:08.080 --> 00:41:09.280
Oh, shut up!

00:41:09.600 --> 00:41:10.840
Oh, stop it...

00:41:19.000 --> 00:41:24.840
In the pursuit of lost love, admitting defeat is never easy.

00:41:26.560 --> 00:41:29.920
She's always loved me, she still loves me.

00:41:29.440 --> 00:41:34.960
When you've been that close to someone it don't wear off.

00:41:34.280 --> 00:41:35.880
It ain't like something you can discard.

00:41:35.040 --> 00:41:38.680
I'm not in love any more, forget it.

00:41:38.400 --> 00:41:46.280
But with the news of another boyfriend, hope fades and old habits return.

00:41:45.400 --> 00:41:48.720
Get rid of them.

00:41:48.680 --> 00:41:55.880
And the mood darkens with a visit from the two of them who have come to pick up her monthly benefit cheque.

00:42:05.960 --> 00:42:07.920
Sorry?

00:42:06.960 --> 00:42:09.800
Are you on this or not?

00:42:09.000 --> 00:42:12.080
No, I don't touch none of it.

00:42:11.280 --> 00:42:13.320
He only drinks.

00:42:12.480 --> 00:42:13.880
Sorry.

00:42:12.960 --> 00:42:17.200
You don't need to apologise for that, I think that's a wise choice.

00:42:18.000 --> 00:42:20.600
It's a shame to see people go down that way.

00:42:19.760 --> 00:42:22.640
It's their lives, isn't it?

00:42:29.280 --> 00:42:33.960
I have to love you and leave you, thanks, bye-bye.

00:42:37.480 --> 00:42:40.080
Don't let yourself go.

00:42:39.880 --> 00:42:44.480
When I ain't got Donna at home it ain't worth being here.

00:42:43.640 --> 00:42:46.360
You'll get her back eventually.

00:42:45.600 --> 00:42:47.800
I don't think that's going to happen.

00:42:47.120 --> 00:42:49.600
Says who?

00:42:48.640 --> 00:42:49.920
You can't...

00:42:49.080 --> 00:42:51.320
Me.

00:42:51.360 --> 00:42:54.760
You don't - you can't say that.

00:42:53.960 --> 00:42:56.280
Don't put yourself down.

00:42:56.240 --> 00:43:00.360
I need the hair of the dog!

00:43:12.080 --> 00:43:16.320
You said you were going to pack it up and you've only got worser.

00:43:15.720 --> 00:43:16.800
That's my opinion.

00:43:15.880 --> 00:43:19.760
I appreciate your opinion, you know I do.

00:43:18.960 --> 00:43:23.080
I can't stop shaking, it's really bad.

00:43:22.360 --> 00:43:25.200
You did say you were going to pack it up, didn't you?

00:43:24.520 --> 00:43:27.320
Yeah, sorry about that.

00:43:27.560 --> 00:43:33.680
I'm not being funny...the scrap, you know what I mean, just go and get it didn't I.

00:43:35.000 --> 00:43:41.920
Those are the times I want to go there and get it because I'm losing out over it.

00:43:41.000 --> 00:43:42.200
We're both losing out.

00:43:41.440 --> 00:43:45.880
Look at yesterday, I had to push you yesterday, didn't I?

00:43:45.080 --> 00:43:49.720
Yesterday around Silverwood Street, you sat down and fell asleep.

00:43:48.760 --> 00:43:51.520
Did I?

00:43:50.600 --> 00:43:52.680
Up the road you were sleeping.

00:43:51.840 --> 00:43:54.800
You can't sleep on the road.

00:43:53.920 --> 00:43:57.120
I must have been so tired.

00:43:56.200 --> 00:44:00.640
Well yours is tired, but you had three goes yesterday at that stuff.

00:43:59.800 --> 00:44:01.440
Three?

00:44:00.640 --> 00:44:02.160
Two or three.

00:44:01.200 --> 00:44:04.760
You're joking!

00:44:03.880 --> 00:44:05.320
You did.

00:44:04.360 --> 00:44:07.720
No wonder I ain't got no money left.

00:44:06.760 --> 00:44:11.680
You were in another world, man, that's the worst I have seen you and that's saying something.

00:44:10.960 --> 00:44:12.440
Oh yeah.

00:44:11.560 --> 00:44:14.800
It's just temptation to you.

00:44:13.880 --> 00:44:19.560
Can't resist it.

00:44:22.880 --> 00:44:25.600
He's got to do it hisself, no-one is going to do it for him.

00:44:26.360 --> 00:44:30.080
He can only be told.

00:44:29.360 --> 00:44:33.200
Whether he listens is another story, innit?

00:44:46.720 --> 00:44:49.840
The battle with drugs goes on.

00:44:49.040 --> 00:44:56.200
For the last resident of Aragon Tower the fight with the council is drawing to a close.

00:44:55.320 --> 00:44:57.920
'Scuse me!

00:44:57.120 --> 00:44:58.160
Arrrgh!

00:44:59.440 --> 00:45:01.720
No, stop!

00:45:08.800 --> 00:45:21.120
In consultation with my solicitor we agreed I should hang on for a buyback price that at least approached the average for a two-bedroom in this area - £175,000 to £180,000.

00:45:20.360 --> 00:45:30.400
Letter from Lewisham Council: "I'm prepared to recommend the council purchase your leasehold interest in Aragon Tower for the sum of £98,000"?

00:45:33.560 --> 00:45:35.880
Perseverance can reap its rewards.

00:45:35.360 --> 00:45:44.840
And after a year alone in the tower, the council have had no choice but to agree to Les's demands.

00:45:44.000 --> 00:45:47.920
I've come out good at the end of a long, hard fight.

00:45:47.120 --> 00:45:51.800
Mixed feelings now because this is finally it, I'm moving.

00:45:52.320 --> 00:46:00.680
I've written in my diary for Monday, "start of a new life - question mark."

00:46:01.440 --> 00:46:07.480
It's pointless getting angry because in the long run it's not going to do me any good.

00:46:06.680 --> 00:46:13.520
This area will be redeveloped quickly now Berkeley Homes have got their foot on this corner.

00:46:14.560 --> 00:46:18.720
I'm calling from Berkeley Homes.

00:46:17.880 --> 00:46:28.120
A little while ago you expressed an interest in the Aragon Tower, or the Z building, and whether you are interested in coming to our prelaunch on - you are, excellent.

00:46:31.640 --> 00:46:36.160
I hope they all apply to these and send them all back.

00:46:35.200 --> 00:46:39.960
770 applicants is quite a good number.

00:46:39.120 --> 00:46:42.560
Blimey, imagine 350 people at the launch.

00:46:41.760 --> 00:46:43.320
Oh my God!

00:47:16.200 --> 00:47:18.720
That is amazing.

00:47:21.640 --> 00:47:28.440
I baptise you in the name of the Lord Jesus Christ for the remission of your sins.

00:47:30.880 --> 00:47:35.240
In the end it will get the better of you, it's only a matter of time.

00:47:34.920 --> 00:47:39.080
How I feel about someone is not your fuckin' business, it's mine.

00:47:41.360 --> 00:47:45.000
This is like somewhere where somebody don't live.

00:47:51.480 --> 00:47:52.960
Thank you.

00:47:52.120 --> 00:47:54.960
I think this is the in-place to be.

00:47:54.000 --> 00:47:56.680
Not only that, living by the river.

00:47:56.000 --> 00:47:58.320
I think you should go for it.
